<onlyinclude>The '''motherboard''' is the main circuit board inside a computer. Also called a mainboard, it mechanically mounts and connects the processor, memory, storage and other devices so they can exchange information and receive power.

== Components and compatibility ==
A desktop motherboard often has a socket for the processor, slots for memory and expansion cards, connectors for drives and external devices, and circuitry that converts incoming power into the voltages components need. Some computers instead solder many components directly to a compact board.

A part fitting into a connector does not guarantee that it will work: the processor socket, memory type, firmware support and electrical interface must also match. The motherboard connects components; the processor executes instructions.


